  "result": "Perfect! All 303 tests pass. The customer merge feature is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` function to `src/customers.js` that:\n\n- Merges a duplicate customer (fromId) into another customer (intoId)\n- Removes the fromId customer from the customers array\n- Reassigns all invoices from fromId to intoId\n- Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with the merged data\n- Normalizes both customer IDs before processing\n- Never mutates original arrays\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Returns `fail('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND')` if either customer doesn't exist\n- Returns `fail('SAME_CUSTOMER')` if both IDs refer to the same customer (after normalization)\n\nAdded 15 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Basic merge functionality\n- Customer removal\n- Invoice reassignment\n- Error handling (fromId not found, intoId not found, same customer)\n- Normalized ID handling (mixed case, whitespace)\n- Array immutability\n- Multiple invoices from same customer\n- Preservation of other customers' invoices\n- Case-insensitive same customer detection",
